READING THIS TABLE:
  * 'ratio' is cpu/gpu wall time. It is a measurement, not a claim, and no gate
    depends on it. §31: qualification does not require GPU speedup.
  * a row is only comparable at all if its equivalence column says BITWISE.
  * the CPU side is SINGLE-THREADED. Against a multi-core CPU implementation the
    ratio would be smaller, and no multi-core CPU density-based path exists to
    measure, so this is not a CPU-vs-GPU hardware comparison.
  * one warm-up GPU step is excluded; context and module load are not charged to
    the timed loop. Host<->device transfer of the initial and final state IS
    excluded from the GPU loop, because advance() is resident by design -- so the
    ratio describes the STEP LOOP, not an end-to-end solve.
